<!DOCTYPE gsdoc PUBLIC "-//GNUstep//DTD gsdoc 1.0.4//EN" "http://www.gnustep.org/gsdoc-1_0_4.dtd">
<gsdoc base="TTIOTransportIngest" stylesheeturl="default-styles.css">
  <head>
    <title>TTIOTransportIngest class documentation</title>
    <author name="Generated by "></author>
    <date>Generated at 2026-06-05</date>
  </head>
  <body>
    <front><contents /></front>
    <chapter>
      <heading>
        Software documentation for the TTIOTransportIngest
        class
      </heading>
      <class name="TTIOTransportIngest" super="NSObject">
        <declared>TTIOTransportIngest.h</declared>
        <desc>
          <p>
            <em>Inherits From:</em> NSObject
          </p>
          <p>
            <em>Declared In:</em> Transport/TTIOTransportIngest.h
          </p>
          <p>
            Incremental transport-stream parser. Maintains
            a rolling byte buffer and emits TTIOTransportPacketRecord
            values to its delegate as packets become complete.
          </p>
          <p>
            Validates everything TTIOTransportReader
            validates — magic, version, header CRC, payload
            CRC when the HasChecksum flag is set, AU-sequence
            monotonicity — but does so packet-by-packet
            instead of in one pass. A failed validation halts
            the ingest; the rolling buffer is discarded and any
            subsequent
            <ref type="method" id="-feed">
              -feed
            </ref>
            returns <code>NO</code>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Not thread-safe: a single ingest instance must be
            driven from one thread. The server pattern is one
            ingest per WS connection, owned by the worker thread
            that accepted the connection.
          </p>
        </desc>
      </class>
    </chapter>
    <chapter>
      <heading>
        Software documentation for the
        TTIOTransportIngestDelegate
        protocol
      </heading>
      <protocol name="TTIOTransportIngestDelegate">
        <declared>TTIOTransportIngest.h</declared>
        <conform>NSObject</conform>
        <desc>
          <p>
            <em>Conforms To:</em> NSObject (NSObject)
          </p>
          <p>
            <em>Declared In:</em> Transport/TTIOTransportIngest.h
          </p>
          <p>
            Receives packets and lifecycle events from a
            TTIOTransportIngest as bytes arrive.
            All callbacks fire on the thread that invoked
            <code>
              <ref type="method" id="-feedBytes:length:error:">
                -feedBytes:length:error:
              </ref>
            </code>
            ; callers managing their own queues (e.g. the workbench
            server's libwebsockets worker thread) should keep
            the work in the callback <strong>short</strong>.
          </p>
        </desc>
        <method type="void">
          <sel>ingest:</sel>
          <arg type="TTIOTransportIngest*">ingest</arg>
          <sel>didFailWithError:</sel>
          <arg type="NSError*">error</arg>
          <desc>
            <em>Description forthcoming.</em>
          </desc>
        </method>
        <method type="void">
          <sel>ingest:</sel>
          <arg type="TTIOTransportIngest*">ingest</arg>
          <sel>didReceivePacket:</sel>
          <arg type="TTIOTransportPacketRecord*">record</arg>
          <desc>
            Fired once per complete packet as it lands in the
            rolling buffer. The callback runs synchronously on
            the thread that invoked ``-feedBytes:length:error:``.
            @param <var>ingest</var> The <var>ingest</var>
            delivering the packet. @param <var>record</var>
            Parsed packet (header + payload).
          </desc>
        </method>
        <method type="void">
          <sel>ingestDidReceiveEndOfStream:</sel>
          <arg type="TTIOTransportIngest*">ingest</arg>
          <desc>
            <em>Description forthcoming.</em>
          </desc>
        </method>
      </protocol>
    </chapter>
  </body>
</gsdoc>
